# Question 01 : 
    Explain the purpose of version control systems like Git. Why are they
    essential in modern software development?

# Answer 01 : 
    A Version Control System (VCS) is a tool that helps developers track and manage changes in source code over time.

    Purpose of Version Control Systems

        1. Track Changes
        It records every change made to the code so developers can see what was modified and when.

        2. Collaboration
        Multiple developers can work on the same project at the same time without overwriting each other's work.

        3. Backup and Recovery
        Previous versions of the code are stored, so if a mistake happens, developers can restore an earlier version.

        4. Branching and Merging
        Developers can create separate branches to work on new features and later merge them into the main project.

    They Are Essential in Modern Software Development

        1. Team Collaboration – Makes it easier for teams to work together on large projects.

        2. Code History – Maintains a complete history of changes.

        3. Error Recovery – Allows developers to revert to earlier working versions.

        4. Project Management – Helps organize and manage large codebases efficiently.

